    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d276">

                <pb facs="0368" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg266"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6125: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-01T15:00:00+08:00">April 1, 1933—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 1—9:30 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>299. Legation’s 295.<anchor n="86" xml:id="d276-f1"/> Following from Mukden:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 31, 4 p.m. According to information from a reliable source the
                            treaty referred to in my telegram of March 30, 3 p.m., provides for the
                            transfer to Japanese control of the Manchukuo telephone, telegraph and
                            wireless systems.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
